e's 'Likely RTL bug' at 30% confidence [evidence:prj-d4a591eb4b.triage.e1] was treated as one candidate, not as proof. Requirement served: [requirement:req-d10c4df532]."}], "files": [{"path": "uart_tx_reload_while_busy_repro_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Self-checking repro: a start pulse while busy must not corrupt the frame in flight", "summary": "Self-checking testbench with no internal signal names. It sends frame 0x3C with no interference, then frame 0xA5 with a 0x5A start pulse early in the DATA phase. It checks the received data, the stop bits and the return to idle against the 8N1 framing and the ignore-while-busy clause of [artifact:prj-d4a591eb4b.design-under-investigation.a1]. It is expected to fail the frame-2 data check on the RTL under investigation and pass on a fixed RTL. A watchdog counts a hang as a failure. It prints one NIRMAAN-SIM verdict with the run nonce just before $finish. Serves [requirement:req-d10c4df532].", "entry": "uart_tx_reload_while_busy_repro_tb"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["The repro is expected to fail exactly one check (frame-2 data) on the RTL under investigation and pass all checks on RTL with the out-of-case hold load removed; this has not been run by me.", "0xA5 and 0x5A differ in every bit, so any data bit sampled after the reload differs from the expected value."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Attempt 1 was refused for listing run IDs in tool_runs that were not recorded. tool_runs is now empty, and no run is claimed. The platform's simulator.run with expect=fail will judge the repro. The independent review is still outstanding and must come from someone other than this seat."}
